AMDGPU Warmfix for Mac Intel (T2, legacy boot)

Stabilizes AMDGPU init on iMac20,2 (i7-10700K + Navi10 / Radeon Pro 5700 XT, Apple T2).
Should also work on other Mac Intel T2 models with AMD GPUs.

Tested in Ubuntu and Fedora.

====================================================================
How it works
====================================================================
- ACPI override (REQUIRED): GFXALT-multi.aml injects PCI fixes at preboot (early initrd).
  Without it, PCI errors appear and GPU init is unreliable.
- Warmfix service: runs a PCI remove/rescan on the AMD slot (.1 audio then .0 VGA).
- Display Manager drop-in: ensures GDM starts only after the warmfix has run.

====================================================================
File overview
====================================================================
- install.sh
  Main installer. Copies scripts/services, generates the PCI reset script,
  builds /boot/acpi_override.img from GFXALT-multi.aml, creates the GDM drop-in.

- amdgpu-reset-pci-template
  Template expanded by the installer into /usr/local/bin/amdgpu-pci-reset-load.sh
  with your GPU PCI slot root (e.g. 03:00).

- amdgpu-pci-reset-load.sh (generated)
  Helper script that removes/rescans AMD GPU PCI functions. Called by warmfix.

- amdgpu-warmfix.service
  Systemd unit that runs the PCI reset at boot, before the display manager.

- t2-gpu-status.sh
  Script to inspect GPU/driver state.

- t2fanrd
  Prebuilt T2 fan controller daemon.
  Source: https://github.com/GnomedDev/T2FanRD

- t2fanrd.service
  Systemd unit to run the fan daemon.

- applesmc-late.service
  Ensures Apple SMC support loads at the right point in boot.

- GFXALT-multi.aml (REQUIRED)
  ACPI table injected at early boot (via acpi_override.img).
  Generated for this project; inspired by Hackintosh methods.
  Reference ACPI repo: https://github.com/t2linux/T2Linux-ACPI
  To regenerate:
      iasl -ve -tc SSDT-GFX0-FIX.dsl
      mv SSDT-GFX0-FIX.aml GFXALT-multi.aml

====================================================================
Install
====================================================================
cd install_gpu
sudo ./install.sh

What it does:
- Builds /boot/acpi_override.img from GFXALT-multi.aml (must be present).
- Installs all *.sh into /usr/local/bin/ and all *.service into /etc/systemd/system/.
- Generates /usr/local/bin/amdgpu-pci-reset-load.sh with correct PCI slot root.
- Adds a display-manager drop-in so GDM starts after warmfix.

Backups of replaced files are suffixed with .bak.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.

====================================================================
GRUB configuration (REQUIRED)
====================================================================
Edit /etc/default/grub and add/adjust:

    GRUB_EARLY_INITRD_LINUX_CUSTOM="acpi_override.img"
    GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX="pci=noaer pcie_aspm=off amdgpu.aspm=0"
    # Remove 'nomodeset' if present (it disables amdgpu)

Then regenerate grub:

    # Legacy boot (iMac T2 and similar)
    sudo grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/grub2/grub.cfg

    # EFI systems (other machines)
    # sudo grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/efi/EFI/fedora/grub.cfg

====================================================================
Verification after reboot
====================================================================
1. ACPI override picked up:
   dmesg | grep -i "ACPI: Early table override"

2. Kernel cmdline includes override:
   cat /proc/cmdline | grep acpi_override.img

3. Warmfix service ran:
   systemctl status amdgpu-warmfix.service --no-pager
   journalctl -u amdgpu-warmfix.service -b --no-pager | tail -n +1

Expected log lines:
- "remove … .1 (audio)"
- "remove … .0 + rescan"

====================================================================
Known issues
====================================================================
- If AMDGPU init fails on the first attempt, the screen may show corruption
  (horizontal line) for ~15–20 seconds. The PCI reset script then retries and
  the driver loads correctly.

- After such an event, rebooting into macOS will usually trigger 1–2 crash
  reports ("remoted" watchdog) and one automatic reboot within the first 5
  minutes. Afterwards macOS runs normally.

- No 5K screen resolution, only up to 4K, limited by AMDGPU.

====================================================================
Troubleshooting
====================================================================
- Booted with nomodeset:
  System falls back to framebuffer (no acceleration). amdgpu-warmfix detects
  nomodeset and exits immediately.

- Black screen (not using nomodeset):
  Check /boot/acpi_override.img, confirm grub params, regenerate grub.cfg.

- Fans spinning at full speed:
  T2 patches not active. Ensure t2fanrd is present in /usr/local/bin/
  and t2fanrd.service is enabled.  Also, T2 Patches required.

- Warmfix didn’t run:
  systemctl status amdgpu-warmfix.service
  Verify drop-in in gdm.service.d/10-amdgpu-warmfix.conf.

- Wrong PCI slot targeted:
  GPU should be always on a fixed slot (example : e.g. 0000:03:00.0(vga) and 0000:03:00.1(audio)).
  Verify with: lspci -nn | grep VGA
  If mismatch, edit amdgpu-pci-reset-load.sh manually.

====================================================================
Notes
====================================================================
- Target system: Fedora 42 on Mac Intel T2 (legacy boot).
- Tested on my iMac20,2.
- Should also work on other T2 Macs with AMD GPUs — feedback welcome!

